You should also look at
http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Bugs_in_NetHack_3.4.3

Some bugs have additional and clarifying information about how to
trigger or what is possibly meant with the bug text.

This sounds like C343-30 "Cursed scroll of destroy armor on cursed
armor doesn't always interact correctly" with the additional info "You
can make the stats gain from putting on an enchantend helm of
brilliance or gloves of dexterity permanent by cursing the armor and
reading cursed destroy armor.".

What I remember from the discussion on IRC and from the answer Alex
got from the DevTeam when this bug got re-discovered that the fix to
C343-30 also should fix this bug. IIRC the fix was adjusting the stats
correctly in Helmet_on/off and Gloves_on/off.

It's not unusual that the DevTeam gets several bug reports about the
same bugs with different approaches on how to trigger them. For
example almost all bugs that refer to potions of acid crashing the
game (and several non-crashing) on the bug list are triggered because
of dangling pointers as the game doesn't correctly tracks destroyed
potions.

I'm not sure if the DevTeam itself trips over the terse bug
descriptions or if they just add new bug descriptions even if the bug
already has a bug number. Could also be a bit of both depending on who
handles a bug report.

